@startuml

title A workload proves which consumer it is before it holds a token

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

participant "systemd\n(the unit)" as systemd
participant "a service\n(no token yet)" as service
participant "ores.vault" as vault
participant "ores.iam" as iam

systemd -> service: LoadCredential: the unit's transport key pair
note right of service
  The private half is a file the platform owns;
  the deployment registered the public half.
end note

service -> vault: challenge(consumer)
vault --> service: nonce, sealed to the consumer's registered key
service -> vault: credential(nonce, name), sealed to the vault's key
vault --> service: the secret, sealed to the consumer's key

service -> iam: sign in with the database password it just resolved
iam --> service: an access token
note right of service
  Every later call is the ordinary token path;
  the bootstrap key is used again at the next start.
end note

@enduml
